  "text": "proprium.immaculatum-cor-beatae-mariae-virginis-postcommunio",
  "about": "The postcommunio of the formulary “Immaculate Heart of the Blessed Virgin Mary” in the 1962 Roman Missal.",
  "segments": {
    "s01": { "translation": "Refreshed by divine gifts, we humbly beseech You, O Lord, that by the intercession of the Blessed Virgin Mary, the solemn feast of whose Immaculate Heart we have celebrated, we may be freed from present dangers and reach the happiness of life eternal. Through our Lord Jesus Christ, Your Son, who lives and reigns with You in the unity of the Holy Spirit, God, forever and ever.", "alignments": [{ "words": ["w041", "w042"], "anchor": "w041", "gloss": "of the Holy Spirit" }] },
    "s02": { "translation": "Amen." }
  },
